# One line-ending policy for every platform: text files check out with LF even on
# Windows (where a global `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise hand every editor and
# formatter CRLF bytes). biome and dprint both compare against LF, so a CRLF working
# tree fails `lint` and `lint:md` for reasons unrelated to any change. `text=auto`
# keeps binary files byte-exact by content detection.
* text=auto eol=lf
